            <div class="scenario-details" id="details-13-6" style="margin-top: 20px; display: block;">
                <div class="details-label">📍 Scenario 13.6 — Battery Heat Assessment (Detailed Guide)</div>
                <div class="details-text">
                    <strong>Why this matters:</strong> Long recording sessions (10 minutes) tax the CPU (Speech Framework) + microphone processing. Excessive heat can trigger thermal throttling or battery drain.
                </div>
                <div class="details-text">
                    <strong>How to assess battery heat:</strong>
                    <ol style="margin-left: 20px; color: #c0c0c0;">
                        <li><strong>Before recording:</strong> Note device temperature by touch (back of phone, near camera). Check Settings > Battery > Battery Health (should be 90%+ health).</li>
                        <li><strong>During recording:</strong> Record 10-minute moment continuously. Monitor battery % — should drop ~2-3% per minute (normal for active app). Speech Framework runs on neural engine, not main CPU.</li>
                        <li><strong>After recording:</strong> Immediately assess:
                            <ul style="margin-top: 8px; margin-left: 20px;">
                                <li>Device temperature — feel back of phone. Should be warm (not hot). Anything above normal hand warmth = concern.</li>
                                <li>Check Settings > Battery to see Dwellable energy impact</li>
                                <li>Allow 2 minutes cooldown, then feel again — temperature should drop</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li><strong>Quality check:</strong> After recording, transcription should complete quickly (WhisperKit runs on-device). If device is too hot, transcription may be slower.</li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
                <div class="details-text">
                    <strong>Pass criteria:</strong>
                    <ul style="margin-left: 20px;">
                        <li>Device becomes warm but not hot (comfortable to hold)</li>
                        <li>Battery drains 20-30% over 10 minutes (expected for active recording)</li>
                        <li>Temperature returns to normal within 2-3 minutes after recording stops</li>
                        <li>Transcription completes in &lt; 30 seconds (no thermal throttling)</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="details-text">
                    <strong>Red flags (report as bug):</strong>
                    <ul style="margin-left: 20px;">
                        <li>Device becomes hot to touch (too uncomfortable to hold to ear)</li>
                        <li>Excessive battery drain (&gt; 50% in 10 minutes)</li>
                        <li>Transcription takes &gt; 60 seconds (suggests thermal throttling)</li>
                        <li>Device thermal shutdown warning appears</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

