                    <th>Pass/Fail</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>5+ failed logins in 10 min</strong></td>
                    <td>Pattern flagged in <code>suspicious_login_patterns</code> view</td>
                    <td>Supabase: <code>SELECT * FROM suspicious_login_patterns WHERE email='test@example.com';</code></td>
                    <td><input type="checkbox"></td>
                </tr>
                <tr style="background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.05);">
                    <td colspan="3"><strong>Notes:</strong> Entry should show email, failed count (5+), lockout_applied=true, last_attempt timestamp</td>
                    <td><input type="checkbox"></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Test 6: Incident Tracking (5 minutes)</h3>
        <p style="color: #c0c0c0; margin-bottom: 15px;"><strong>Objective:</strong> Verify that security incidents are created and tracked.</p>
        <table class="reference-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Action</th>
                    <th>Expected Incident Entry</th>
                    <th>Verification</th>
                    <th>Pass/Fail</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>5+ failed logins trigger incident</strong></td>
                    <td>Row created in <code>abuse_incidents</code> with severity='medium' or 'high'</td>
                    <td>Supabase: <code>SELECT * FROM abuse_incidents WHERE incident_type='brute_force' ORDER BY created_at DESC LIMIT 1;</code></td>
                    <td><input type="checkbox"></td>
                </tr>
                <tr style="background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.05);">
                    <td colspan="3"><strong>Notes:</strong> Check status is 'open', email matches test account, timestamp is recent</td>
                    <td><input type="checkbox"></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Test 7: Rate Limiting (Advanced) (5 minutes)</h3>
        <p style="color: #c0c0c0; margin-bottom: 15px;"><strong>Objective:</strong> Verify API rate limiting (100 calls/min per user) is working.</p>
        <table class="reference-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Scenario</th>
                    <th>Expected Behavior</th>
                    <th>Result</th>
                    <th>Pass/Fail</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Normal API usage</strong></td>
                    <td>All API calls succeed (fetch moments, save, etc.)</td>
                    <td><input type="text" placeholder="All operations completed normally"></td>
                    <td><input type="checkbox"></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Excessive API calls (advanced)</strong></td>
                    <td>After 100+ calls/min: Rate limit error appears</td>
                    <td><input type="text" placeholder="If you manually test this: '429 Too Many Requests' or similar"></td>
                    <td><input type="checkbox"></td>
                </tr>
                <tr style="background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.05);">
                    <td colspan="3"><strong>Note:</strong> Normal testing (fetch, save, etc.) won't hit this. Only if you write a script to hammer the API.</td>
                    <td><input type="checkbox"></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Test 8: App Stability & No Crashes (5 minutes)</h3>
        <p style="color: #c0c0c0; margin-bottom: 15px;"><strong>Objective:</strong> Verify no crashes occur during security testing.</p>
        <table class="reference-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Test Scenario</th>
                    <th>Expected Result</th>
                    <th>Actual Result</th>
                    <th>Pass/Fail</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>App crashes during brute force test?</strong></td>
                    <td>NO — App remains stable, shows error messages gracefully</td>
                    <td><input type="text" placeholder="No crashes observed"></td>
                    <td><input type="checkbox"></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>App crashes during lockout?</strong></td>
                    <td>NO — Lockout timer ticks down smoothly</td>
                    <td><input type="text" placeholder="Lockout UI stable, no freezing"></td>
                    <td><input type="checkbox"></td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>App crashes during multi-account switch?</strong></td>
                    <td>NO — Account switching works smoothly</td>
                    <td><input type="text" placeholder="Sign out → sign in works reliably"></td>
                    <td><input type="checkbox"></td>
                </tr>
                <tr style="background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.05);">
                    <td><strong>OVERALL SECURITY TESTING STATUS</strong></td>
                    <td colspan="2">All 8 tests passed?</td>
                    <td><input type="checkbox"></td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <div style="background: rgba(76, 175, 80, 0.1); border-left: 4px solid #4cb50; padding: 15px; margin-top: 30px; margin-bottom: 20px; border-radius: 4px;">
            <h3 style="color: #4cb50; border: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 10px 0;">Security Testing Sign-Off</h3>
            <p style="color: #c0c0c0; margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>Tester Name:</strong> <input type="text" placeholder="Your name" style="padding: 5px; width: 200px;"></p>
            <p style="color: #c0c0c0; margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>Date:</strong> <input type="date" style="padding: 5px; width: 150px;"></p>
            <p style="color: #c0c0c0; margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>Device:</strong> <input type="text" placeholder="iPhone 13 Pro Max, etc." style="padding: 5px; width: 200px;"></p>
            <p style="color: #c0c0c0; margin-bottom: 10px;"><strong>Overall Result:</strong>
                <select style="padding: 5px; width: 150px;">
                    <option>---</option>
                    <option>✅ ALL PASS - Ready for TestFlight</option>
                    <option>⚠️ SOME ISSUES - Document below</option>
                    <option>❌ CRITICAL ISSUES - Do not release</option>
                </select>
            </p>
            <p style="color: #c0c0c0;"><strong>Issues Found (if any):</strong></p>
            <textarea placeholder="Document any issues, failures, or concerns..." style="width: 100%; height: 100px; padding: 10px; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); color: #e0e0e0; border: 1px solid #d4af37; border-radius: 4px;"></textarea>
        </div>

        <div class="actions">
            <button onclick="exportResults()">📋 Export Results</button>
            <button onclick="resetForm()" class="secondary">🔄 Clear Form</button>
        </div>

        <div class="footer">
            <p>Dwellable Master Testing Checklist — Updated March 17, 2026 (Evening)</p>
            <p>15 Phases | 65 Scenarios | Build 106 TestFlight | Phase 15: Pre-TestFlight Security Testing (8 tests)</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        function switchTab(e, tabName) {
            e.preventDefault();

            // Hide all tabs
            const contents = document.querySelectorAll('.tab-content');
            contents.forEach(content => content.classList.remove('active'));

            // Remove active from all buttons
            const buttons = document.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn');
            buttons.forEach(btn => btn.classList.remove('active'));

            // Show selected tab
            document.getElementById(tabName).classList.add('active');
            e.target.classList.add('active');
        }

        function toggleDetails(btn) {
            const row = btn.closest('tr');
            const details = row.nextElementSibling?.querySelector('.scenario-details');
            if (details) {
                details.classList.toggle('show');
                btn.textContent = details.classList.contains('show') ? 'Hide' : 'Details';
            }
        }

        function exportResults() {
            alert('Export feature: Copy all form data to clipboard or file.\n\nNote: This is a template. Implement export functionality as needed.');
        }

        function resetForm() {
            if (confirm('Clear all form entries? This cannot be undone.')) {
                document.querySelectorAll('input, textarea').forEach(el => el.value = '');
            }
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
